.Dd October 20, 2026
.Dt CRATE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm crate
.Nd containerizer for FreeBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a containerizer for FreeBSD that packages applications and services
into isolated, self-contained containers
.Pq Pa .crate No files
and runs them in dedicated FreeBSD jails with automatic networking, firewall,
and resource cleanup.
Containers contain everything needed to run the containerized software \(em
only the
.Nm
executable and the FreeBSD kernel are required at runtime.
.Ss Commands
.Bl -tag -width "snapshot"
.It Cm create Fl s Ar spec.yml Fl o Ar output.crate
Create a container from a YAML specification.
Optionally use
.Fl -template Ar name
for template inheritance.
Use
.Fl -use-pkgbase
for FreeBSD 16+ pkgbase bootstrap.
.It Cm run Fl f Ar file.crate Op Fl - Ar args
Run a container.
Arguments after
.Fl -
are passed to the containerized application.
The jail is named after the file name up to its first
.Ql \&. ,
so that part must be 1\(en128 characters from
.Ql [A-Za-z0-9._-]
.Pq the same rule as Fl -name ;
otherwise
.Cm run
refuses the file before creating anything
.Pq e.g.\& rename Pa my app.crate No to Pa my-app.crate .
.It Cm validate Fl s Ar spec.yml
Validate a specification file for syntax and logical consistency.
.It Cm snapshot Ar subcommand
Manage ZFS snapshots:
.Cm create , list , restore , delete , diff .
.It Cm list Op Fl j
List running containers in table or JSON format.
.It Cm info Ar target
Show detailed information about a running container.
.It Cm console Ar target Op Fl u Ar user
Open an interactive shell in a running container.
.It Cm clean Op Fl n
Clean up orphaned resources.
Use
.Fl n
for dry-run.
.It Cm export Ar target Op Fl o Ar file
Export a running container to a
.Pa .crate
archive with SHA256 validation.
Only the jail's own root filesystem is archived
.Pq Fl -one-file-system :
host directories and files shared into the jail, GUI sockets and
.Pa /dev
are mounted filesystems and stay out (since 1.1.48).
.It Cm import Ar file Op Fl o Ar file Op Fl -force
Import a
.Pa .crate
archive with integrity validation.
.It Cm gui Ar subcommand
GUI session manager:
.Cm list , focus , attach , url , tile , screenshot , resize .
.It Cm stack Ar subcommand Ar stack.yml
Multi-container stacks:
.Cm up , down , status , exec .
See
.Sx STACK FILES .
.It Cm stats Op Fl j Ar target
Resource usage of one container
.Pq CPU%, memory, PIDs, I/O, network .
.It Cm logs Ar target Op Fl f
Show
.Pq Fl f : follow
the container console log.
.It Cm stop Ar target
Stop a running container
.Pq SIGTERM, then the jail is removed .
.It Cm restart Ar target
Stop and start again from the recorded
.Pa .crate
file and variables.
.It Cm top
Live resource monitor across all running containers
.Pq the DISK column is the write rate, Sy writebps , not usage .
.It Cm inter-dns
Rebuild the global
.Pa .crate
DNS zone from the running jails.
.It Cm vpn Ar subcommand
VPN tooling:
.Cm wireguard render-conf Ar spec.yml ,
.Cm ipsec render-conf Ar spec.yml .
.It Cm inspect Ar target
Full JSON snapshot of a running container's state.
.It Cm migrate Ar target Fl -from Ar endpoint Fl -to Ar endpoint
Move a container between hosts through the
.Xr crated 8
API.
.It Cm backup Ar target Fl -output-dir Ar dir
ZFS send stream of the jail dataset
.Pq incremental with Fl -incremental-from .
.It Cm backup-prune Ar dir Fl -keep Ar spec
Delete old
.Pa .zstream
files by retention bucket.
.It Cm restore Ar stream Fl -to Ar dataset
Replay a backup stream into a fresh dataset.
.It Cm replicate Ar target Fl -to Ar host Fl -dest-dataset Ar dataset
Stream a ZFS snapshot to a remote host over
.Xr ssh 1 .
.It Cm template warm Ar target Fl -output Ar dataset
Capture a jail's on-disk state as a warm template.
.It Cm retune Ar target Fl -rctl Ar key=value ...
Live-tune RCTL limits of a running jail
.Pq Fl -show , Fl -clear .
.It Cm throttle Ar target Fl -ingress Ar rate Fl -egress Ar rate
Dummynet token-bucket shaping of the jail's traffic.
.It Cm doctor Op Fl j
Host health check: kernel modules, commands, ZFS, firewall, racct,
jails.
.It Cm vm-wrap Ar vm Fl -jail Ar name
Render a devfs ruleset and
.Pa jail.conf
for a
.Xr bhyve 8
enclosure.
.It Cm update Ar target Fl -pkg-only
In-place
.Xr pkg 8
upgrade inside a running jail
.Pq Fl n dry-run, Fl y auto-yes .
.It Cm profile-from-trace Oo Fl o Ar spec Oc Fl - Ar command Op Ar args ...
Run the command once on the host, unsandboxed, under
.Xr truss 1
and write a minimal specification draft from what it opened, executed,
connected to and listened on: executed
.Pa /usr/local
programs become
.Sy pkg/install ,
files under the home
.Sy dirs/share
and
.Sy files/share ,
X11 and D-Bus sockets, GPU, video and certificate files the matching
options, destinations
.Sy options/net/outbound ,
listening sockets
.Sy inbound-tcp
and
.Sy inbound-udp .
What cannot be mapped is left as a comment.
.Fl -trace-file Ar file
reads a saved trace instead of running;
.Fl -keep-trace Ar file
keeps the raw one.
.It Cm audit Ar target Oo Fl j Oc Oo Fl -offline Oc Op Fl -dns Ar name
What a running container can actually reach, seen from the inside.
One
.Xr sh 1
probe runs in the jail with base-system tools only and its output
becomes the PASS/WARN/FAIL table of
.Cm doctor :
securelevel, hostname and hostid compared with the host's, the
.Sy allow.*
flags as the jail sees them, host paths visible through nullfs
(read-write or read-only), device classes in
.Pa /dev
(gpu, video, sound, input, usb, serial, disks, raw), interfaces and the
default route, inet listeners, host unix sockets reachable (X11, D-Bus,
Wayland, sound), who runs what, one TCP connect to the default gateway
and one DNS lookup.
WARN marks an exposure worth a look, not an error.
.Fl -offline
skips the two network probes,
.Fl -dns
picks the name looked up (default
.Li www.freebsd.org ) .
Needs root or the crated privops socket, like
.Cm console .
Exit status 0, 1 (a WARN) or 2 (the probe did not run).
.El
