.Sh SPECIFICATION FORMAT
Container specifications are YAML files with the following top-level keys:
.Ss Base system
.Bl -tag -width "keep-wildcard"
.It Sy base/mode
.Cm full
.Pq default
or
.Cm host-ro .
With
.Cm full
the container carries a complete copy of the FreeBSD base system
.Pq trimmed by Sy base/keep No and Sy base/remove .
With
.Cm host-ro
.Pq thin jail, 1.1.58
the container carries only the writable layer
.Pq Pa /etc /var /root /tmp /home /usr/local
extracted from the base archive of the host's release, and
.Cm run
nullfs-mounts the host's own userland directories read-only into the jail
before it starts:
.Pa /bin /sbin /lib /libexec /rescue
and
.Pa /usr/bin /usr/sbin /usr/lib /usr/lib32 /usr/libexec /usr/libdata /usr/share /usr/include .
The archive is a few megabytes, the start skips the big extraction, and a
host upgrade upgrades every thin jail at its next start.
.Pa /usr/local
stays per container and writable, so
.Sy pkg/install
and
.Cm update Fl -pkg-only
work as usual.
The directory list is frozen into the
.Pa +CRATE.THIN
manifest inside the archive together with the host release; a thin jail
started on a host of another release branch gets a warning
.Pq its Pa /etc No was generated for the other release .
.Sy base/keep , base/keep-wildcard
and
.Sy base/remove
have no effect in this mode.
Not compatible with
.Fl -use-pkgbase .
.Cm export
of a running thin jail archives the writable layer only
.Pq Fl -one-file-system
and yields a valid thin crate.
.It Sy base/host-dirs
.Pq host-ro only
List of host directories to mount instead of the default list above.
Each entry must be an absolute, normalised path; the root directory,
.Pa /usr
itself
.Pq it would hide the container's Pa /usr/local
and anything in the writable layer are refused, as are nested entries.
.Pa /usr/lib32 , /rescue
and
.Pa /usr/include
may be absent on the host and are then skipped; any other missing
directory is an error.
.It Sy base/keep
Files and directories to keep from the base system.
.It Sy base/keep-wildcard
Glob patterns to keep.
.It Sy base/remove
Files and directories to remove.
.El
.Ss Packages
