.Bl -tag -width "command"
.It Sy run/command
Executable path with optional arguments.
.It Sy run/service
Services to run (list or scalar).
.El
.Ss Shared resources
.Bl -tag -width "files/share"
.It Sy dirs/share
Directories shared between host and jail.
Each entry is a path (same on both sides) or a pair
.Pq from, to .
.It Sy files/share
Files shared between host and jail.
Same format as
.Sy dirs/share .
.El
.Ss Options
The
.Sy options
key accepts a list
.Pq simplified format
or a map
.Pq extended format .
Supported options:
.Cm net , x11 , ssl-certs , tor , video , gl , no-rm-static-libs ,
.Cm dbg-ktrace , wireguard , ipsec .
.Pp
See
.Sx NETWORKING
for details on the
.Cm net
option.
.Bl -tag -width "wireguard/config"
.It Sy options/wireguard/config
Path of a
.Xr wg-quick 8
configuration on the host; the interface is brought up inside the
jail's vnet at start and torn down at exit.
.Cm crate vpn wireguard render-conf
renders the file from the spec.
.It Sy options/ipsec/conn
Name of a strongSwan
.Ic conn
to bring up
.Pq Ic ipsec auto --up
before the jail starts and down at teardown.
.It Sy options/ipsec/conf
Optional path of a conn snippet on the host that is installed into
.Pa strongswan.d/
.Pq followed by Ic ipsec reread
before the conn is used.
.El
.Ss Security
.Bl -tag -width "enforce_statfs"
.It Sy security/securelevel
Jail securelevel, \-1 to 3
.Pq default: 2 .
.It Sy security/children_max
Maximum child jails
.Pq default: 0 .
.It Sy security/cpuset
CPU pinning
.Pq e.g., \(dq0-3\(dq, \(dq0,2,4\(dq .
.It Sy security/enforce_statfs
Filesystem visibility: 0, 1, or 2.
.It Sy security/allow_quotas
Allow filesystem quotas.
.It Sy security/allow_set_hostname
Allow changing hostname.
.It Sy security/allow_chflags
Allow changing file flags.
.It Sy security/allow_mlock
Allow memory locking.
.El
.Ss Resource limits
The
.Sy limits
key is a map of RCTL resource names to values.
Supported resources:
.Cm cputime , datasize , stacksize , coredumpsize , memoryuse ,
.Cm memorylocked , maxproc , openfiles , vmemoryuse , pseudoterminals ,
.Cm swapuse , nthr , msgqqueued , msgqsize , nmsgq , nsem ,
.Cm nsemop , nshm , shmsize , wallclock , pcpu , readbps ,
.Cm writebps , readiops , writeiops .
.Bl -tag -width "disk_quota"
.It Sy limits/disk_quota
ZFS
.Sy refquota
for the container dataset: an integer followed by
.Cm K , M , G
or
.Cm T
.Pq e.g.\& 10G .
Requires
.Sy zfs_enable .
.El
.Ss IPC
.Bl -tag -width "raw_sockets"
.It Sy ipc/sysvipc
Enable System V IPC (shared memory, semaphores, message queues).
.It Sy ipc/mqueue
Enable POSIX message queues.
.It Sy ipc/raw_sockets
Control raw socket access.
.El
.Ss Encryption
.Bl -tag -width "keyformat"
.It Sy encrypted
Boolean or map.
When a map:
.It Sy encrypted/method
Encryption method
.Pq only \(dqzfs\(dq supported .
.It Sy encrypted/keyformat
Key format:
.Cm passphrase , hex , raw .
.It Sy encrypted/cipher
Cipher:
.Cm aes-256-gcm , aes-256-ccm , aes-128-gcm , aes-128-ccm .
.El
.Ss Copy-on-Write
.Bl -tag -width "backend"
.It Sy cow/mode
.Cm ephemeral
.Pq rollback on exit
or
.Cm persistent
.Pq retain changes .
.It Sy cow/backend
.Cm zfs
.Pq default
or
.Cm unionfs .
.El
.Ss DNS filtering
.Bl -tag -width "redirect_blocked"
.It Sy dns_filter/allow
Whitelist patterns.
.It Sy dns_filter/block
Blacklist patterns (wildcard).
.It Sy dns_filter/redirect_blocked
IP address or
.Dq nxdomain .
.El
.Ss Firewall policy
.Bl -tag -width "default"
.It Sy firewall/block-ip
CIDR ranges to block.
.It Sy firewall/allow-tcp
TCP ports to allow.
.It Sy firewall/allow-udp
UDP ports to allow.
.It Sy firewall/default
Default policy:
.Cm allow
or
.Cm block .
.El
.Pp
The policy is loaded into the per-jail pf anchor
.Pa crate/<jail>
in NAT mode and, since 1.1.38, in bridge mode when the jail's IPv4
address is known at start (a static
.Sy ip
or a
.Sy network_pool
allocation). With DHCP addressing there is no address to anchor the
rules on and the policy is skipped with a warning. The anchor is
flushed at teardown in every mode.
.Ss GUI
.Bl -tag -width "vnc_password"
.It Sy gui/mode
.Cm nested , headless , gpu , auto , wayland
or
.Cm compositor .
.Cm wayland
is the strict-Wayland counterpart to
.Cm auto :
no X11 fallback, refuses to start if WAYLAND_DISPLAY is unset.
.Cm compositor
runs a Wayland compositor
.Em inside
the jail
.Pq Sy gui/compositor
and exposes it through
.Xr wayvnc 1 .
.It Sy gui/resolution
Display resolution
.Pq e.g., \(dq1920x1080\(dq .
.It Sy gui/vnc
Enable x11vnc.
.It Sy gui/vnc_port
VNC port number.
.It Sy gui/novnc
Enable noVNC/websockify.
.It Sy gui/vnc_password
VNC password.
.It Sy gui/gpu_device
PCI Bus ID for GPU mode.
.It Sy gui/gpu_driver
Driver:
.Cm nvidia , amdgpu , intel ,
or
.Cm dummy .
.It Sy gui/backend
For
.Cm compositor
mode:
.Cm headless
.Pq default; wlroots headless backend
or
.Cm drm
.Pq a GPU is passed in .
.It Sy gui/compositor
Command run as the in-jail compositor in
.Cm compositor
mode, e.g.\&
.Dq sway
or
.Dq cage firefox .
Required for that mode.
.It Sy gui/vnc_bind
Address
.Xr wayvnc 1
listens on.
Default
.Ar 127.0.0.1 ;
anything else exposes an unauthenticated desktop to that network.
.It Sy gui/vnc_native
Use the embedded libvncserver instead of forking
.Xr x11vnc 1
.Pq needs a build with Ev WITH_LIBVNCSERVER ; falls back with a warning otherwise .
.El
.Ss X11 isolation
A top-level
.Sy x11
map replaces the plain
.Cm x11
option when the display sharing mode matters:
.Bl -tag -width "resolution"
.It Sy x11/mode
.Cm shared
.Pq the host display, default ,
.Cm nested
.Pq a Xephyr window
or
.Cm none .
.It Sy x11/resolution
Size of the nested display
.Pq default 1280x720 .
.It Sy x11/clipboard
Boolean; default true.
.El
.Pp
.Sy x11: true
is accepted as the short form of the option; any other scalar is
rejected.
.Ss Clipboard
.Bl -tag -width "direction"
.It Sy clipboard/mode
.Cm isolated , shared ,
or
.Cm none .
.It Sy clipboard/direction
.Cm in , out , both ,
or
.Cm none .
.El
.Ss D-Bus
.Bl -tag -width "policy"
.It Sy dbus/system
Enable system bus.
.It Sy dbus/session
Enable session bus.
.It Sy dbus/policy/allow_own
Service names to allow owning.
.It Sy dbus/policy/deny_send
Service names to deny sending to.
.El
.Ss Managed services
.Bl -tag -width "auto_start"
.It Sy services/managed
List of services (each with
.Sy name , enable , rcvar
fields).
.It Sy services/auto_start
Auto-start on container run.
.El
.Ss Scheduled jobs
.Bl -tag -width "cron/schedule"
.It Sy cron
List of periodic jobs run by
.Xr cron 8
inside the container.
Each entry is a map with the fields below;
.Sy schedule
and
.Sy command
are required.
When at least one entry is present,
.Nm
writes the crontab and sets
.Ql cron_enable="YES"
in the container's
.Pa /etc/rc.conf .
.It Sy cron/schedule
A
.Xr crontab 5
time specification, e.g.\&
.Ql 0 3 * * * .
.It Sy cron/command
The command line to run.
.It Sy cron/user
User whose crontab receives the jobs; default
.Ql root .
Must be 1\(en32 characters from
.Ql [A-Za-z0-9._-] ,
must not start with
.Ql - ,
and must not be
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql .. ;
anything else is rejected before the container starts
.Pq the value becomes a file name under Pa /var/cron/tabs/ .
.Pp
Entries are grouped by
.Sy user
and written to one crontab per user under
.Pa /var/cron/tabs/
inside the container.
.El
.Ss Socket proxying
.Bl -tag -width "proxy"
.It Sy socket_proxy/share
Host socket paths to share via nullfs.
Each path is mirrored at the same path inside the container, and that
container-side path must resolve inside the container's root \(em a
value that escapes it
.Pq e.g.\& with Ql ..
is rejected.
.It Sy socket_proxy/proxy
List of proxy entries with
.Sy host , jail , direction
fields.
The
.Sy jail
path must likewise resolve inside the container's root;
.Sy host
is a host-side path chosen by the operator and is not confined.
.El
.Ss Terminal
.Bl -tag -width "allow_raw_tty"
.It Sy terminal/devfs_ruleset
Devfs ruleset number (0-65535) of the operator's own rules.
Since 1.1.62 it is
.Em included
into the jail's private ruleset in place of the built-in base (see
.Sx Devices ) ;
the device classes are added on top.
.It Sy terminal/allow_raw_tty
Allow raw TTY access.
.El
.Ss Devices
What the jail's
.Pa /dev
shows (1.1.62).
Every jail gets a private
.Xr devfs 8
ruleset: everything hidden, then the basic nodes
.Pq null, zero, random, urandom, crypto, tty, ptmx, pts/*, fd/*, stdin/stdout/stderr, fuse, zfs ,
.Pa bpf*
with the
.Sy net
option, then the classes named here.
Before 1.1.62 a jail without
.Sy terminal/devfs_ruleset
saw the host's whole
.Pa /dev .
.Bl -tag -width "serial"
.It Sy devices/sound
.Pa dsp* , mixer* , sndstat , audio* , midi* .
.It Sy devices/gpu
.Pa dri , dri/* , drm/* , nvidia* .
Implied by the
.Sy gl
option and the
.Sy gui
gpu, auto and compositor modes.
.It Sy devices/video
.Pa video*
(cameras).
Implied by the
.Sy video
option.
.It Sy devices/input
.Pa input/*
(evdev: keyboards, mice).
Everything typed on the host is readable from inside; implied by the
compositor's drm backend.
.It Sy devices/usb
.Pa usb/* , usbctl , ugen* , uhid* , u2f* :
every USB device of the host.
.It Sy devices/serial
.Pa cua* , ttyu* , ttyU* .
.El
.Pp
Forms:
.Dl devices: {sound: true, gpu: true}
.Dl devices: [sound, gpu]
.Dl devices: all
The last keeps the host's whole
.Pa /dev
visible (the pre-1.1.62 behaviour);
.Nm crate validate
warns about it and about input, usb and serial.
.Nm crate audit
shows the resulting view from inside.
.Ss Advanced security
.Bl -tag -width "mac_bsdextended"
.It Sy security_advanced/capsicum
Enable Capsicum capability mode.
.It Sy security_advanced/mac_bsdextended
List of ugidfw rules.
.It Sy security_advanced/mac_portacl/allow_ports
Port binding restrictions.
The rules are merged into the host-wide
.Va security.mac.portacl.rules
list when the container starts and removed from it again when it
stops; rules other containers or the operator added are left alone
(since 1.1.44 — earlier releases overwrote the whole list).
.It Sy security_advanced/hide_other_jails
Prevent enumeration of other jails.
.El
.Ss Lifecycle hooks
.Bl -tag -width "run:before-start-services"
.It Sy scripts/create:begin
Before container creation.
.It Sy scripts/create:end
After container creation.
.It Sy scripts/run:begin
Before container execution.
.It Sy scripts/run:after-create-jail
After jail is created.
.It Sy scripts/run:before-start-services
Before services start.
.It Sy scripts/run:before-execute
Before main command execution.
.It Sy scripts/run:after-execute
After main command exits.
.It Sy scripts/run:end
After container shutdown.
.El
.Ss Health check
.Bl -tag -width "start_period"
.It Sy healthcheck
Either a command string
.Pq the short form
or a map.
The command runs inside the jail as root; exit status 0 means
healthy.
Service-only containers are monitored in the background and the
state is shown by
.Cm crate list
and
.Cm crate stats .
.It Sy healthcheck/test
The command.
Required in the map form.
.It Sy healthcheck/interval
Seconds between checks; default 30, must be at least 1.
.It Sy healthcheck/timeout
Seconds before a check counts as failed; default 5.
.It Sy healthcheck/retries
Consecutive failures before the container is marked unhealthy;
default 3.
.It Sy healthcheck/start_period
Grace period in seconds before the first check; default 0.
.El
.Ss Restart policy
.Bl -tag -width "max_retries"
.It Sy restart
.Pq alias Sy restart_policy
Either the policy name or a map.
.Cm no
.Pq default ,
.Cm on-failure
.Pq restart when the application exits non-zero ,
.Cm always
or
.Cm unless-stopped .
.Cm crate run
stops restarting after
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM
in every policy.
.It Sy restart/policy
The policy name.
.It Sy restart/max_retries
Restarts before giving up; default 3.
.It Sy restart/delay
Seconds between restarts; default 5, must be at least 1.
.El
.Ss Dependencies
.Bl -tag -width "depends"
.It Sy depends
List of container names this one needs.
Only
.Cm crate stack
acts on it: containers are started in dependency order and stopped
in reverse; a plain
.Cm crate run
ignores the list.
.El
.Ss Base container
.Bl -tag -width "base_container/name"
.It Sy base_container
Clone the root filesystem from an existing running jail
.Pq a ZFS clone of its dataset
instead of bootstrapping a base system.
.It Sy base_container/type
Only
.Cm jail
is supported
.Pq default .
.It Sy base_container/name
Jail name or JID to clone from.
Required.
.El
.Ss ZFS datasets
.Bl -tag -width "zfs/datasets"
.It Sy zfs/datasets
Datasets
.Pq e.g.\& Pa tank/data
to attach to the jail with
.Ic zfs jail .
The container needs
.Sy security/allow_quotas
or
.Sy security_advanced
privileges as appropriate to manage them from inside.
Requires
.Sy zfs_enable .
.El
.Sh NETWORKING
.Nm
supports four network modes for containers, configured via the
.Sy mode
field in
.Sy options/net .
All modes use VNET
.Pq Xr vnet 9
for network virtualization.
.Ss Network modes
.Bl -tag -width "passthrough"
.It Cm nat
.Pq default
Epair virtual interface with ipfw NAT.
Automatic 10.0.0.0/8 IP assignment, outbound traffic control
.Pq wan/lan/host/dns ,
and inbound port forwarding.
IPv6 ULA (fd00:cra7:e::/48) pass-through via
.Sy ipv6: true .
.It Cm bridge
Epair attached to an existing
.Xr if_bridge 4
interface.
Supports DHCP
.Pq Sy ip: dhcp ,
static IP
.Pq Sy ip: 192.168.1.50/24 ,
VLAN tagging, static MAC, and IPv6 SLAAC.
Requires the
.Sy bridge
field
.Pq e.g., bridge: bridge0 .
.It Cm passthrough
Physical network interface passed directly into the jail via
.Xr vnet 9 .
The interface is reclaimed when the container exits.
Supports DHCP, static IP, VLAN, static MAC, and IPv6 SLAAC.
Requires the
.Sy interface
field.
.It Cm netgraph
.Xr ng_bridge 4
with
.Xr ng_eiface 4 .
Alternative to
.Cm bridge
mode for L2 networking.
Requires the
.Sy interface
field for the physical interface.
.El
.Ss Network option fields
.Bl -tag -width "static-mac"
.It Sy network
Reference to a named network defined in the system configuration.
See
.Sx NAMED NETWORKS .
.It Sy mode
.Cm nat , bridge , passthrough ,
or
.Cm netgraph .
Default:
.Cm nat .
.It Sy bridge
Bridge interface name for
.Cm bridge
mode
.Pq e.g., bridge0 .
.It Sy interface
Physical interface for
.Cm passthrough
or
.Cm netgraph
modes.
.It Sy ip
IP addressing:
.Cm dhcp , none ,
or a static address in CIDR notation
.Pq e.g., 192.168.1.50/24 .
.It Sy gateway
Gateway IP address (only with static IP).
.It Sy ip6
IPv6 addressing:
.Cm slaac , none ,
or a static IPv6 address.
.It Sy static-mac
Generate deterministic MAC address using SHA-256
.Pq vendor OUI 58:9c:fc
over the jail name and interface name, so the same container gets
the same MAC on every run (since 1.1.38; earlier releases hashed a
per-run name and the MAC changed each start).
.It Sy vlan
802.1Q VLAN ID, 1-4094.
Only valid with
.Cm bridge , passthrough ,
or
.Cm netgraph
modes.
.It Sy outbound
.Pq NAT mode only
List of allowed outbound targets:
.Cm wan , lan , host , dns , all , none .
.It Sy inbound-tcp , inbound-udp
.Pq NAT mode only
Port forwarding rules.
Map of external port/range to internal port/range.
.It Sy ipv6
.Pq NAT mode only
Enable IPv6 ULA pass-through
.Pq boolean .
.It Sy extra
List of additional interfaces, each with the same fields as above
.Pq except Sy outbound No and Sy inbound .
.El
.Sh NAMED NETWORKS
Reusable network profiles can be defined in the system configuration file
under the
.Sy networks
key.
Container specifications reference them via
.Sy network: Ar name
in the
.Sy options/net
section.
Named network fields serve as defaults \(em explicit values in the container
specification always override.
.Pp
Example system configuration:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/crate.yml
networks:
    external:
        mode: bridge
        bridge: bridge0
        gateway: 192.168.1.1
        static-mac: true
    internal:
        mode: bridge
        bridge: bridge1
        gateway: 10.0.0.1
        vlan: 100
.Ed
.Pp
Example container specification using named networks:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
options:
    net:
        network: external
        ip: 192.168.1.50/24
        extra:
            - network: internal
              ip: 10.0.0.50/24
.Ed
.Pp
Named network definition fields:
.Bl -tag -width "static-mac"
.It Sy mode
.Cm bridge , passthrough ,
or
.Cm netgraph .
.It Sy bridge
Bridge interface name.
.It Sy interface
Physical interface.
.It Sy gateway
Gateway IP address.
.It Sy vlan
VLAN ID (1-4094).
.It Sy static-mac
Deterministic MAC generation.
.It Sy ip6
IPv6 mode:
.Cm slaac , none ,
or static address.
.El
.Sh STACK FILES
.Cm crate stack
starts several containers from one YAML file; containers are started
in dependency order and stopped in reverse.
Each
.Cm crate run
is spawned as its own detached process and the stack waits for its
jail to appear.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
containers:
  postgres:
    spec: postgres.yml            # or crate: postgres.crate
    vars: { PG_VERSION: "16" }
  webapp:
    spec: webapp.yml
    template: web-base            # optional --template for the build
    depends: [postgres]
    vars:
      DB_HOST: "postgres"
      DB_PASSWORD: { from_file: /usr/local/etc/secrets/db }
    volumes: [certs:/etc/letsencrypt:ro]

volumes:
  certs: /usr/local/etc/letsencrypt

networks:
  backend:
    bridge: bridge10
    subnet: 10.99.0.0/24
    gateway: 10.99.0.1
    ip_range: 10.99.0.100-10.99.0.200
    dns: true

network_policy:
  default: deny
  rules:
    - { from: webapp, to: postgres, proto: tcp, ports: [5432], action: allow }
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "network_policy"
.It Sy containers/<name>
One container.
Exactly one of
.Sy spec
.Pq a specification built on the fly
or
.Sy crate
.Pq an existing archive
is required.
The name follows the jail-name rule
.Pq 1\(en128 characters from Ql [A-Za-z0-9._-] .
.It Sy containers/<name>/depends
Start-order dependencies inside the stack.
.It Sy containers/<name>/vars
Variables substituted as
.Li ${KEY}
in the spec; a map with
.Sy from_file
reads the value from a host file
.Pq trailing newline stripped .
.Fl -var Ar KEY=VALUE
on the command line overrides.
.It Sy containers/<name>/volumes
.Li name:/path[:ro]
mounts of the stack-level
.Sy volumes .
.It Sy volumes
Named host directories
.Pq a path, or a map with Sy path .
.It Sy networks
Bridges the stack creates when missing.
.Sy bridge
is required;
.Sy subnet
is an IPv4 CIDR and
.Sy gateway
a bare address assigned to the bridge;
.Sy ip_range
.Pq Ar first-last
is the pool containers without a static address draw from;
.Sy dns: true
starts a stack-local resolver that answers the container names.
Names follow the jail-name rule.
.It Sy network_policy
Inter-container firewall rules loaded into the host
.Xr ipfw 8
.Pq Sy net.link.bridge.ipfw is enabled .
.Sy default
is
.Cm allow
or
.Cm deny ;
each rule names
.Sy from
and
.Sy to
containers, an optional
.Sy proto
and
.Sy ports
list, and an
.Sy action .
Rule numbers are taken from a free block above the live rules and
removed by
.Cm stack down .
.El
.Pp
.Cm stack exec Ar stack.yml name Fl - Ar cmd
runs a command in the jail whose name is exactly
.Ar name
.Pq plus the Li _pid<N> suffix crate appends ;
a container named
.Ar db
never matches
.Ar mydb .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
reads configuration from YAML files in the following order
.Pq higher priority wins :
.Bl -enum
.It
.Pa /usr/local/etc/crate.yml
\(em system-wide configuration.
.It
.Pa /usr/local/etc/crate.d/*.yml
\(em drop-in fragments, loaded in alphabetical order.
.It
.Pa ~/.config/crate/crate.yml
\(em per-user overrides (highest priority).
.El
.Ss Configuration keys
.Bl -tag -width "compress_xz_options"
.It Sy prefix
Jail directory root.
Default:
.Pa /var/run/crate .
.It Sy cache
Cache directory.
Default:
.Pa /var/cache/crate .
.It Sy logs
Log directory.
Default:
.Pa /var/log/crate .
.It Sy zfs_enable
Enable ZFS integration.
Default: false.
.It Sy zfs_zpool
ZFS pool name.
.It Sy zfs_options
ZFS dataset creation options.
Default:
.Dq -o compress=lz4 -o atime=off .
.It Sy network_interface
Default network interface for gateway detection.
Auto-detected if empty.
.It Sy default_bridge
Default bridge interface for
.Cm bridge
mode when not specified in spec.
.It Sy static_mac_default
Enable deterministic MAC by default for non-NAT modes.
Default: false.
.It Sy network_pool
IPv4 CIDR from which
.Cm network: auto
jails receive a static address and the pool's first host address as
gateway
.Pq e.g. Dq 10.66.0.0/16 .
Empty (default) falls back to DHCP on the bridge.
.It Sy network_pool6
IPv6 ULA prefix for the same purpose
.Pq e.g. Dq fd00:0:0:1::/64 .
.It Sy network_pool_user_bits
Rootless only (1.1.39): each operator allocates from a per-uid
sub-block this many bits narrower than
.Sy network_pool
(a /16 pool with the default 8 gives every uid a /24; the sub-block
must stay at /28 or wider). 0 shares one pool between operators, who
may then receive the same address because lease files are per user.
Default: 8.
.It Sy network_pool6_user_bits
Same for
.Sy network_pool6 .
Default: 16.
.It Sy firewall_backend
.Cm pf , ipfw , none
or empty (auto-detect via
.Xr kldstat 8 ,
pf preferred) for the SNAT/rdr auto-rules of
.Cm network: auto .
.It Sy bootstrap_method
Base system bootstrap method.
Default:
.Dq base_txz .
.It Sy securelevel
Default securelevel for specs that leave
.Sy security/securelevel
at \-1 (auto).
Default: unset (\-1, the jail inherits the host's securelevel).
Since 1.1.46; earlier releases documented this key but never read it.
.It Sy children_max
Default
.Va children.max
for specs that leave
.Sy security/children_max
at \-1 (auto).
Default: unset (\-1, kernel default).
Since 1.1.46.
.It Sy search_path
List of directories to search for
.Pa .crate
files.
Default:
.Dq \&. ,
.Pa ~/.local/share/crate ,
.Pa /usr/local/share/crate .
.It Sy compress_xz_options
XZ compression options.
Default:
.Dq -T0 .
.It Sy networks
Named network definitions.
See
.Sx NAMED NETWORKS .
.El
.Sh TEMPLATES
Built-in templates in
.Pa templates/ :
.Bl -tag -width "network-isolated"
.It Pa standard.yml
NAT with WAN and DNS access, shared Downloads directory.
.It Pa development.yml
NAT with full outbound, shared home directory, SysV IPC, allow_mlock.
.It Pa minimal.yml
Bare jail with no network or X11.
.It Pa privacy.yml
Tor proxy, ZFS encryption, ephemeral COW, DNS filtering.
.It Pa network-isolated.yml
No network, nested X11 at 1280x720.
.It Pa bridge-dhcp.yml
Bridge mode with DHCP and static MAC.
.It Pa bridge-static.yml
Bridge mode with static IP and gateway.
.It Pa passthrough.yml
Passthrough mode with DHCP and IPv6 SLAAC.
.It Pa netgraph.yml
Netgraph mode with DHCP and static MAC.
.El
.Pp
Since 1.1.59 the template and the specification are merged at the YAML
level (template first, specification on top; see
.Sx PROFILES
for the rules) and the merged document is what the archive carries in
.Pa +CRATE.SPEC ,
so the template's settings reach
.Cm crate run .
.Sh PROFILES
.Cm crate run Ar name
without
.Fl f
looks a specification up by name, first match wins:
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/share/examples/crate/" -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/crate/profiles/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .yml
the operator's own profiles
.It Pa /usr/local/share/crate/profiles/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .yml
site-local profiles (directory created by the operator)
.It Pa /usr/local/share/examples/crate/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .yml
the examples shipped with crate
.El
.Pp
The archive is built on first use into
.Pa ~/.local/share/crate/profiles/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .crate
and reused; it is rebuilt when the profile or its
.Pa .local
is newer.
The build is a
.Cm crate create ,
which needs root: an unprivileged operator is told the exact
.Cm crate create Fl s Ar merged Fl o Ar archive
recipe for root (the merged specification is already written) and runs
normally once the archive exists.
The jail is named after the profile, exactly as with
.Fl f Ar name Ns Pa .crate .
Profile names follow the jail-name rule
.Pq Li [A-Za-z0-9._-] ,
may not start with
.Ql -
or
.Ql \&.
and may not end in
.Pa .local .
.Pp
An optional
.Pa ~/.config/crate/profiles/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa .local.yml
is merged on top of the profile: maps key by key, lists appended without
duplicates,
.Sy options
by option name whichever form each file uses, scalars replaced by the
override.
A
.Pa .local
may add packages, options, limits, run arguments and shares under
.Ev $HOME ;
it may not contain the top-level keys
.Sy security_advanced , dbus , base , scripts , encrypted , securelevel ,
.Sy socket_proxy ,
nor a
.Sy dirs/share
or
.Sy files/share
host path outside the operator's home directory.
Such an override is refused with the reason; copy the profile into
.Pa ~/.config/crate/profiles/
and edit the copy instead.
The merged specification is written next to the archive as
.Ar name Ns Pa .yml
(generated, do not edit) and is what
.Pa +CRATE.SPEC
contains.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/crate.d/*.yml"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/crate.yml
System-wide configuration.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/crate.d/*.yml
Drop-in configuration fragments.
.It Pa ~/.config/crate/crate.yml
Per-user configuration.
.It Pa ~/.config/crate/profiles/
Per-user profiles and
.Pa <name>.local.yml
overrides; see
.Sx PROFILES .
.It Pa /usr/local/share/crate/profiles/
Site-local profiles.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/crate/profiles/
Archives and merged specifications built from profiles.
.It Pa /var/run/crate/
Runtime jail directories and context files.
.It Pa /var/cache/crate/
Cache directory.
.It Pa /var/log/crate/
Log directory.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create and run a container:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
crate create -s examples/firefox.yml -o firefox.crate
crate run -f firefox.crate
.Ed
.Pp
Create with template inheritance:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
crate create -s app.yml --template development.yml -o app.crate
.Ed
.Pp
List running containers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
crate list
crate list -j    # JSON output
.Ed
.Pp
Container with bridge networking:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# spec.yml
options:
    net:
        mode: bridge
        bridge: bridge0
        ip: dhcp
        static-mac: true
.Ed
.Pp
Container with multiple interfaces using named networks:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# spec.yml
options:
    net:
        network: external
        ip: 192.168.1.50/24
        extra:
            - network: internal
              ip: 10.0.0.50/24
.Ed
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
.Nm
supports FreeBSD 13.0 and later (13.x, 14.x, 15.x).
All version-specific features have safe fallback code paths.
.Pp
FreeBSD 15.0 adaptations (automatic, no user action needed):
.Bl -bullet
.It
JAIL_OWN_DESC \(em race-free jail removal via owning descriptor.
Falls back to
.Fn jail_remove
on older kernels.
.It
Epair checksum offload fix \(em txcsum/txcsum6 disabled unconditionally
(harmless on 13.x/14.x).
.It
OS version mismatch detection \(em warns when host and container
FreeBSD major versions differ.
.It
ipfw compatibility warning \(em alerts when a FreeBSD 15 host runs
a container built with an older base.
.El
.Pp
All network modes require VIMAGE support in the kernel
.Pq Sy kern.features.vimage=1 .
This is a
.Xr loader.conf 5
tunable.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jail 8 ,
.Xr ipfw 8 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr vnet 9 ,
.Xr if_bridge 4 ,
.Xr ng_bridge 4 ,
.Xr rctl 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5
.Sh BUGS
Inbound network ports cannot be accessed from the host running the container
due to a FreeBSD bug
.Pq PR 239590 .
They can only be accessed from other hosts.
